<article class="env-lemma" id="0BXY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BXY">Lemma <span data-tag="0BXY">53.2.1</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $X$ be a curve and $Y$ a proper variety. Let $U \subset X$ be a nonempty open and let $f : U \to Y$ be a morphism. If $x \in X$ is a closed point such that $\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$ is a discrete valuation ring, then there exist an open $U \subset U' \subset X$ containing $x$ and a morphism of varieties $f' : U' \to Y$ extending $f$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a special case of Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/0BX7" data-tag="0BX7">29.43.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>